 # Chibi toolchain consolidation and self-hosting
 
+## Ordinary Chibi CLI application and shared program sessions, 2026-10-28
+
+The owner approved making the public CLI an ordinary Chibi application with
+Main and a shared compiler/runtime interface. The isolated worktree started at
+2c6d3ed5c and is now on codex/chibi-main-app-20261028 at accepted origin/main
+51650ccff, with all changes carried forward without conflicts. The validated
+authored-runner candidate is preserved in
+.chibi/main-runner-reload/authored-runner-preservation; the original checkout
+and both earlier checkpoints remain intact.
+
+Move all public command routing, argument validation, watching, retry, exit
+policy, game-cache decisions and subprocess construction into apps/chibi.
+Install that package with the SDK. The native chibi_main.c only resolves the
+application/core resources, starts the ordinary application host and returns
+its Main result. Remove the private Run entry, runner.* pack and compiler --run
+bridge rather than retaining a second route. Program arguments are ordinary
+application argv, allowing chibi apps/chibi -- version to run the CLI itself.
+
+Export Chibi::program beside source_catalog. An explicit program session owns
+candidate/accepted generations and structured diagnostics, accepts an immutable
+source snapshot, native declarations/bindings/backend/services, and exposes
+transactional preparation/replacement plus synchronous invocation. This gives
+Studio's native host an interface for unsaved document snapshots without file
+polling or terminal policy. The authored program service owns checked session
+handles, independent argv and a small open/update/call/diagnostic/close interface.
+CLI and user programs use this same service. Existing compiler and runtime
+replacement remain the source of truth; no second compiler or migration engine.
+
+Generic application services expose OS/file/process/network operations. Native
+project adapters expose typed inspection/export and SDK identity facts. No
+native callback parses command argv. Catalogs/services outlive their sessions;
+caller/target heaps stay distinct, active/reentrant sessions reject mutation,
+invalid drafts preserve the accepted generation, and cancellation tears down
+owned sessions, listeners and temporary directories. Compiler services remain
+outside deployed game catalogs. Windows file/path loading must work for the
+new application startup rather than regressing previously native CLI commands.
+
+Changes include apps/chibi, authoring/program{,_service}, host/application{,
+_io,_tools}, the tiny launcher, ordinary catalog composition, SDK/CMake/graph
+resource and link ownership, source reader portability, focused tests and
+documentation. Studio packaging must carry application resources when copying
+the public executable. Studio UI changes are outside this increment.
+
+Verify all public commands, authored argument tests, nested CLI execution,
+multiple session handles, buffer snapshots, retained-state reload and rejected
+edits, cancellation/cleanup, installed SDK C consumers, graph/CMake resource
+parity and relocation. Select native language/CLI/export/native-build/packaging
+checks for the affected behavior, report actual times, and cross-compile the
+Windows paths when native execution is unavailable. Record remaining coverage
+and final results below after implementation.
+
+Accepted-base progress: native release graph build passes in 135.4s plus 2.2s
+dependency preparation. Shared/runtime selectors pass 279 cases / 22,410
+assertions in 2.168s combined subprocess time, including 7 program-session
+cases. POSIX source/path selectors pass 23 / 15,851 in 2.570s runner time.
+The public-header-only SDK consumer passes 1 / 13 in 0.271s; graph/CMake
+application resource parity passes 2 / 20 in 51.338s. The actual CLI runs its own
+six authored tests and can invoke itself through the normal program path with
+byte-identical version output. Initial CLI integration passed 28/31; three new
+fixtures used invalid dynamic assertion messages, now corrected for retry.
+Full public SDK installation/export validation is still pending; the private
+compiler-tools SDK does not establish it. Native Windows execution is unrun;
+strict MinGW release syntax passes for nine production files and the Windows
+filesystem fixture. Linux graph link-order parity is not established here.
+
+Independent review fixed drive/UNC root handling, empty argv, temporary-prefix
+ownership, worker-safe signal polling and test-runtime argv registration. The
+launcher admits standard reflected value layouts so native vector defaults
+remain valid. Cooperative outer invocation keeps cleanup and status decisions
+in Main; nested calls are interruptible. No C command dispatcher remains.
+
+## Main runner and state-preserving reload, 2026-10-28
+
+Port the local Main runner onto origin/main at 2c6d3ed5c in an isolated
+worktree. Preserve the original checkout and its tracked/untracked changes;
+the backup is .chibi/hello-port-preservation-20261028 in that checkout.
+
+The CLI supports explicit run and file/directory shorthand. Installed
+tools/toolchain/Run.chibi owns run-request parsing, the opt-in --watch loop,
+revision suppression, compile/prepare/commit decisions and exit-status policy.
+Private native capabilities supply source snapshots, compiler/runtime handles,
+diagnostics, signals and waits. They are absent from user-program catalogs.
+The native launcher still routes public commands and paths.
+
+The host keeps an execution_program alive between Main calls. Runtime-owned
+invocation binds retained state and imports. Existing prepare/commit replacement
+owns state migration, resets and retired generations. Invalid edits retain the
+accepted generation. Ordinary locals reinitialize; retain locals persist. Main
+remains synchronous. Policy and user code execute in separately owned runtimes
+and managed heaps, with no borrowed values crossing their invocation boundary.
+
+Changes cover the source loader, program authoring host, runtime function-call
+boundary, CLI/compiler dispatch, both build descriptions, documentation and
+native boundary regressions. No syntax, project-version or Studio change.
+
+Verify Main file/directory execution, exit status and diagnostics; retained
+state across valid reloads, invalid-edit recovery and import changes; current
+publication, record-publication and root-state/runtime coverage. Build against
+this worktree's matching compiler/runtime. Record actual results and elapsed
+time; do not infer new-main readiness from the old runner's test results.
+
+The preserved native-orchestration checkpoint against 2c6d3ed5c passed its
+release build. CLI: 28 cases,
+398 assertions, 13.856 seconds. Native runtime: program 211/14,167/1.519s,
+publication 6/320/1.047s, record-publication 7/230/1.046s, root-state
+3/194/1.036s, modules 22/908/0.830s. All passed; runtime call/reload cases
+exercise bytecode and the platform compiled backend. Manual watch printed
+Run 1 then Reloaded 2 in one process. Clang-format 22 and diff checks passed.
+Full native/material/project/language/tooling aggregates, browser/Windows and
+Studio were not run. No SDK installation or publishing occurred.
+
+The authored-policy candidate replaces that C watch loop. Its release build
+passes (149 seconds for the initial graph build; subsequent incremental builds
+passed, most recently 15.0 seconds plus 2.3 seconds of dependency configuration).
+CLI: 29 cases, 424 assertions, 14.931 seconds. Runtime: program 211/14,167/1.668s,
+publication 6/320/1.318s, record-publication 7/230/1.322s, root-state
+3/194/1.282s, modules 22/908/1.374s. Graph/CMake resource parity: 2/20/54.115s.
+SDK packaging and relocation: 8/214/293.815s. All pass, including numeric
+retained-state migration, invalid-edit recovery, imported state, required
+installed-policy loading and isolation of private capabilities. Two earlier
+CLI attempts caught diagnostic wording changes; both original entry-error
+oracles now pass. Logs and attempt history are in .chibi/main-runner-reload.
+
+Manual Hello World and watch output Run 1 then Reloaded 2 pass through the
+authored policy. All four unchanged authored parser tests pass through the
+private host with a disposable entry wrapper. Independent ownership/phase
+review, clang-format 22 and diff checks pass. Broader aggregates, browser,
+Windows and Studio remain unrun. The user's installed SDK remains unchanged.
+The prior native checkpoint is preserved under
+.chibi/main-runner-reload/c-host-preservation in this worktree.
+
